$FG,5$$TX+CX,"Haile Selassie I — Address to the United Nations"$$FG$

$FG,2$Date:$FG$    4 October 1963
$FG,2$Venue:$FG$   United Nations General Assembly, New York
$FG,2$Context:$FG$ Delivered during the 18th session of the UN General
          Assembly, three months after Selassie's founding role at
          the Organisation of African Unity in Addis Ababa. The
          address gives Rastafari thought its most-cited civic text,
          and was later adapted by Bob Marley into the song "War."
          ZionOS quotes from the original speech, not from the song.

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,2$Selected passages$FG$

  $FG,3$"Until the philosophy which holds one race superior and
   another inferior is finally and permanently discredited and
   abandoned ..."$FG$

  $FG,3$"Until the color of a man's skin is of no more significance
   than the color of his eyes ..."$FG$

  $FG,3$"We must become members of a new race, overcoming petty
   prejudice, owing our ultimate allegiance not to nations but to
   our fellow men ..."$FG$

  $FG,3$"Peace is a day-to-day problem, the product of a multitude of
   events and judgements. Peace is not an 'is', it is a 'becoming.'"$FG$

  $FG,3$"The real issue is whether [conflicts] are to be resolved by
   force, or by resort to peaceful methods and procedures."$FG$

  $FG,3$"If we are to survive, this Organization must survive. To
   survive, it must be strengthened."$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

